@*
    Shown once Include attachments is on for a site whose last test didn't confirm the attachment
    permission: what to add, where to add it, and the guide's entry. The permission is asked for
    here, when the feature that needs it is turned on, rather than up front for every site.
*@

<div id="@Id" class="alert alert-warning py-2 small mt-2 mb-0" role="status">
    <span class="bi-exclamation-triangle me-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <strong>Attachments need one more permission.</strong>
    The last test of @(SiteName ?? "this site") didn't confirm <code>@Scope</code>,
    so attachments would be skipped while @(Scope == ConfluenceSpaceSelection.AttachmentScope ? "pages" : "issues") and comments keep syncing. To add it:
    <ol class="mb-1 mt-1 ps-3">
        <li>
            In <a href="https://admin.atlassian.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Atlassian Administration<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>,
            create a new OAuth 2.0 credential on the service account with the site's scopes plus
            <code>@Scope</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
            <a id="@($"{Id}-replace")" href="@ConfluenceSpaceSelection.ReplaceCredentialsUrl(ConnectionId)" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Replace credentials on @(SiteName ?? "the site")<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
            with the new client ID and secret. Connapse tests them first and records the permission.
        </li>
    </ol>
    <a id="@($"{Id}-guide")" href="@ConfluenceSpaceSelection.MissingScopeGuideUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Missing scope in the setup guide<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Id { get; set; } = "";

    /// <summary>The site connection whose credential needs the permission.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public Guid ConnectionId { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? SiteName { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The permission to add: Confluence's unless a Jira source asks for its own.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Scope { get; set; } = ConfluenceSpaceSelection.AttachmentScope;
}
